### WCF Appointment Service REST API Tests with Correlation Tracking
### Base URL - Update the port number to match your local development server
@baseUrl = http://localhost:63124
@serviceUrl = {{baseUrl}}/AppointmentService.svc

### 1. Get All Appointments (with correlation headers)
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
X-Correlation-Id: get-all-001
X-Consumer-Id: http-test-client
X-User-Id: tester@example.com
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get Specific Appointment by ID (with correlation headers)
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments/1
X-Correlation-Id: get-one-001
X-Consumer-Id: http-test-client
X-User-Id: tester@example.com
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Get Appointment by ID 2
GET {{serviceUrl}}/appointments/2
X-Correlation-Id: get-two-001
X-Consumer-Id: http-test-client
X-User-Id: tester@example.com
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Create New Appointment - With Headers
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
X-Correlation-Id: create-001
X-Consumer-Id: mobile-app
X-User-Id: doctor@hospital.com
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "Title": "Follow-up Consultation",
  "Description": "Follow-up appointment for test results review",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-20T10:00:00",
  "Location": "Room 303",
  "PatientName": "Michael Johnson",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Williams",
  "DurationMinutes": 30
}

###

### 5. Create New Appointment - With Body Parameters (No Headers)
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "ConsumerId": "web-portal",
  "UserId": "admin@hospital.com",
  "Title": "Cardiology Appointment",
  "Description": "Annual heart health checkup and EKG",
  "AppointmentDate": "2024-12-25T14:30:00",
  "Location": "Cardiology Department - Room 501",
  "PatientName": "Sarah Davis",
  "DoctorName": "Dr. Anderson",
  "DurationMinutes": 60
}

###

### 6. Create New Appointment - Emergency (Both Headers and Body)
POST {{serviceUrl}}/appointments
X-Correlation-Id: emergency-001
X-Consumer-Id: emergency-system
